subject: Bundle the Japanese DevTools locale

DevTools only ships the en-US and zh locales inside the bundled
frontend. Every other locale, including ja, is fetched at runtime from
the remote devtools://devtools/remote endpoint. The Android build
blocks that endpoint (the built-in frontend is the only one that can
load), so choosing Japanese in the DevTools settings always failed to
load the ja locale data and DevTools silently fell back to en-US.

Move ja from remote_devtools_locales to bundled_devtools_locales and
add front_end/core/i18n/locales/ja.json to grd_files_bundled_sources,
the same treatment zh already gets, so the Japanese locale data is
packed into the build and DevTools loads it locally.
---
diff --git a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/i18n.gni b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/i18n.gni
--- a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/i18n.gni
+++ b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/i18n.gni
@@ -42,5 +42,4 @@
   "is",
   "it",
-  "ja",
   "ka",
   "kk",
@@ -91,4 +90,5 @@
 bundled_devtools_locales = [
   "en-US",
+  "ja",
   "zh",
 ]
diff --git a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/devtools_grd_files.gni b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/devtools_grd_files.gni
--- a/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/devtools_grd_files.gni
+++ b/third_party/devtools-frontend/src/config/gni/devtools_grd_files.gni
@@ -331,4 +331,5 @@
   "front_end/core/i18n/i18n.js",
   "front_end/core/i18n/locales/en-US.json",
+  "front_end/core/i18n/locales/ja.json",
   "front_end/core/i18n/locales/zh.json",
   "front_end/core/platform/api/api.js",
